From: chelovechishee <261262090+chelovechishee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 21/43] ASoC: samsung: abox: keep the DSP on, defer DSP
 component controls, 64K RDMA buffer

- probe by default (snd_soc_abox.enable=0 keeps it off); keep ABOX
  runtime-active: without the DISPAUD domain driver nothing calls
  abox_disable_callback(), and each runtime resume re-ran abox_enable()
  over the running DSP (failsafe, random hangs when PipeWire starts)
- DSP component controls (ERAP info, Forte Media) are added once the
  card is bound; their values, the sampling rates, RDMA synchronization,
  ERAP and sound type are cached and sent only to a running DSP, and
  restored when it boots
- the DSP wraps the RDMA position at 64 KiB: limit the playback buffer
- routes of the missing UAIF4/DSIF go to their AIF widgets; guard the
  component work against an unbound card

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
